The numbers 1 to {n} are each coloured blue or red. Determine {k} possible colourings that satisfy the following rules:

\begin{{enumerate}}
\item The number {n} is red.
\item If numbers $x$ and $y$ have different colours and $x + y \leqslant {n}$, then $x + y$ is blue.
\item If numbers $x$ and $y$ have different colours and $x \cdot y \leqslant {n}$, then $x + y$ is red.
\end{{enumerate}}

